WEBVTT

00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:16,830
heard that high dose melatonin is good for before a scan was radiation.

00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:23,870
Yeah, I've heard that before. I don't know that you can really

00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:29,070
prove that though. That's the difficult thing about something like that because you can't

00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:35,150
really measure your rad dose of radiation, the damage, the tissues.

00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:45,470
So, you know, it's like, oh, take high dose melatonin. There's some sense to it from a

00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:53,470
metabolic pathway, but it's possible to really prove that because you can't measure

00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:59,630
the damage, the post-damage radiation, somebody who hasn't taken it, somebody who has taken it,

00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:03,630
but that is something that you can't really. Certainly high dose melatonin can be

00:01:03,630 --> 00:01:13,630
beneficial for cancer in itself, and taking that before bed. We have some patients that are

00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:24,260
taking 100 milligrams of melatonin, you know, before they go to bed. Thank you, you can send that to me.

00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:28,340
Yeah, I read some things about it, but it's hard to measure that.

